IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vca-core`
IMPORT `vca-seat`

-- Cases for the prescribed maxima (reg 4), their indexation by the Hobart CPI, and the question "What is the most I can
-- be awarded for this application" (ss 5(10), 6A). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited Act and
-- Regulations, never copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comments.
--
-- The CPI figures below are HYPOTHETICAL, chosen so the arithmetic is exact; they are not the ABS's figures, which are
-- not deposited. Quarterly, from the March quarter 2020:
--   2020: 100, 100, 100, 100           average 100
--   2021: 101, 102, 102, 103           average 408 / 4 = 102
--   2022: 106, 107, 107.2, 108.2       average 428.4 / 4 = 107.1
--   2023: 102, 102, 102, 102           average 102 (a fall)
--   2024: 107, 107, 107.2, 107.2       average 428.4 / 4 = 107.1
--   2025: 109.242 in each quarter      average 109.242
-- Percentage change for the financial year starting 1 July (reg 4(1)):
--   2022: (102 - 100) / 100 = 2%; 2023: (107.1 - 102) / 102 = 5.1 / 102 = 5%; 2024: (102 - 107.1) / 107.1, about
--   -4.76%; 2025: (107.1 - 102) / 102 = 5%; 2026: (109.242 - 107.1) / 107.1 = 2.142 / 107.1 = 2%.
-- Maxima (reg 4(2)(b), (3)(b)): each year x (1 + change), but never below the year before (so 2024-25 holds):
--   primary, single offence:  30 000; 30 600; 32 130; 32 130; 33 736.50; 34 411.23
--   primary, more than one:   50 000; 51 000; 53 550; 53 550; 56 227.50; 57 352.05
--   secondary victim:         20 000; 20 400; 21 420; 21 420; 22 491;    22 940.82
--   related victim, funeral:  10 000; 10 200; 10 710; 10 710; 11 245.50; 11 470.41
-- for the financial years ending 30 June 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026 and 2027.

`the test CPI` MEANS
    LIST 100, 100, 100, 100,
         101, 102, 102, 103,
         106, 107, 107.2, 108.2,
         102, 102, 102, 102,
         107, 107, 107.2, 107.2,
         109.242, 109.242, 109.242, 109.242

-- The same figures, but only through the December quarter 2024.
`the test CPI to 2024` MEANS
    LIST 100, 100, 100, 100,
         101, 102, 102, 103,
         106, 107, 107.2, 108.2,
         102, 102, 102, 102,
         107, 107, 107.2, 107.2

`single` MEANS `a primary victim where there is a single offence (reg 4(2)(a)(i))`
`series` MEANS `a primary victim where there is more than one offence (reg 4(2)(a)(ii))`
`secondary` MEANS `a secondary victim (reg 4(2)(a)(iii))`
`related` MEANS `a related victim (reg 4(2)(a)(iv))`
`funeral cap` MEANS `funeral expenses (reg 4(3))`

`the PV`        MEANS `a primary victim (s 2)`
`the SV witness` MEANS `a secondary victim injured by witnessing the offence (s 2, para (a))`
`the SV parent` MEANS `a secondary victim as parent, step-parent or guardian of a primary victim under 18 (s 2, para (b))`
`the RV`        MEANS `a related victim (s 2)`
`the FP`        MEANS `a person who incurred a primary victim's funeral expenses (s 4(1A))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. The core: financial years, averages, percentage changes and maxima (reg 4).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A financial year is named by the year it starts: 30 June 2025 is in 2024-25, 1 July 2025 in 2025-26.
#ASSERT `the financial year starting in` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2025) EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT `the financial year starting in` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the financial year starting in` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 12 2021) EQUALS 2021

#ASSERT `the average Hobart CPI for the 4 quarters ending 31 December` 2021 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 102
#ASSERT `the average Hobart CPI for the 4 quarters ending 31 December` 2022 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 107.1
#ASSERT `the percentage change for the financial year starting 1 July` 2022 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the percentage change for the financial year starting 1 July` 2023 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the percentage change for the financial year starting 1 July` 2024 `from` `the test CPI` LESS THAN 0
#ASSERT `the percentage change for the financial year starting 1 July` 2025 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the percentage change for the financial year starting 1 July` 2026 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 2

-- The 2021-22 figures (reg 4(2)(a), (3)(a)).
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `single` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2021 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `series` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2021 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `secondary` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2021 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `related` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2021 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `funeral cap` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2021 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 10000

-- Primary victim, single offence, each year.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `single` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2022 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 30600
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `single` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2023 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 32130
-- 2024-25: the CPI fell, so 32 130 x (1 - 4.76%) = 30 600 is "less than the prescribed maximum for the immediately
-- preceding financial year": 32 130 holds (reg 4(2)(b)(ii)).
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `single` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2024 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 32130
-- 2025-26: the 5% rise is applied to the 32 130 that was held: 33 736.50. Following the CPI from the base would give
-- 30 000 x 107.1 / 100 = 32 130 (NOTES.md finding 13).
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `single` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2025 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 33736.5
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `single` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2025 `from` `the test CPI` GREATER THAN 30000 TIMES (107.1 DIVIDED BY 100)
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `single` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2026 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 34411.23
-- The other classes in 2025-26 and 2026-27.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `series` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2025 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 56227.5
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `series` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2026 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 57352.05
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `secondary` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2025 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 22491
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `secondary` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2026 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 22940.82
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `related` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2025 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 11245.5
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `related` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2026 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 11470.41
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `funeral cap` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2025 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 11245.5
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum for` `secondary` `in the financial year starting 1 July` 2024 `from` `the test CPI` EQUALS 21420

-- Whether the figures reach a year: 2026-27 needs the 2025 quarters (24 figures); the list to 2024 has 20.
#ASSERT `the figures reach the financial year of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026) `in` `the test CPI`
#ASSERT NOT (`the figures reach the financial year of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026) `in` `the test CPI to 2024`)
#ASSERT `the figures reach the financial year of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) `in` `the test CPI to 2024`
-- 2021-22 needs no figures at all.
#ASSERT `the figures reach the financial year of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2022) `in` EMPTY

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. "What is the most I can be awarded for this application" (ss 5(10), 6A(1)-(4)). Arguments: kind; number of
-- offences; date lodged; date decided; CPI figures; already awarded for the same conduct.
-- =====================================================================================================================

`1 Mar 2024`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2024
`1 Sep 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025
`1 Mar 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026
`1 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026
`1 Mar 2022`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2022
`1 Aug 2022`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2022
`1 Nov 2021`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2021
`1 Dec 2021`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2021
`15 Dec 2021` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 12 2021
`30 Jun 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2025
`1 Jul 2024`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2024

-- Alex, primary victim of a single offence, lodges 1 March 2024 (2023-24: 32 130) and is decided 1 September 2025
-- (2025-26: 33 736.50): "the greater of" the two (s 5(10)) = 33 736.50. Future services may be paid on top (s 6A(4)).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Mar 2024` `1 Sep 2025` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 33736.5 TRUE
-- Lodged 1 March 2022 (2021-22: 30 000), decided 1 August 2022 (2022-23: 30 600): 30 600.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Mar 2022` `1 Aug 2022` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 30600 TRUE
-- Lodged 1 July 2024 (2024-25: 32 130, held), decided 30 June 2025 (also 2024-25): 32 130. Lodged in 2023-24 and decided
-- in 2024-25 gives 32 130 too: the greater of 32 130 and 32 130.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Jul 2024` `30 Jun 2025` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 32130 TRUE
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Mar 2024` `30 Jun 2025` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 32130 TRUE
-- Decided 1 September 2026 (2026-27: 34 411.23), with the figures through 2025; with figures only to 2024, not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Sep 2026` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 34411.23 TRUE
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Sep 2026` `the test CPI to 2024` 0 EQUALS `not covered: the Hobart CPI figures given do not reach the financial year needed`
-- Lodged 1 November 2021, before the Regulations took effect, decided 1 March 2022: at least 30 000; the maximum under
-- the earlier regulations at lodgement is not deposited and would win if higher (s 5(10)(a); NOTES.md finding 14).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Nov 2021` `1 Mar 2022` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `at least this much: the maximum when I lodged, before 15 December 2021, was set by earlier regulations that are not deposited (s 5(10)(a))` 30000 TRUE
-- Decided 1 December 2021: before 15 December 2021, not covered. Decided on 15 December 2021 itself: 30 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Nov 2021` `1 Dec 2021` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `not covered: determined before 15 December 2021, under regulations that are not deposited`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `15 Dec 2021` `15 Dec 2021` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 30000 TRUE
-- Alex already has a $5 000 interim award for the same conduct (s 5(6)): "the total amount ... awarded ... in respect
-- of any particular criminal conduct" (s 6A(1)), so 33 736.50 - 5 000 = 28 736.50 is left (NOTES.md finding 17).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Mar 2024` `1 Sep 2025` `the test CPI` 5000 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 28736.5 TRUE
-- Three offences by the same offender, a series (s 6A(2)(b)): reg 4(2)(a)(ii), 2025-26: 56 227.50.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 3 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 56227.5 TRUE
-- Two assaults by two offenders not acting in concert are two "particular criminal conduct"s, each with the single
-- offence maximum: 33 736.50 each, 67 473 in all, more than the 56 227.50 for a series (NOTES.md finding 16).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 33736.5 TRUE
#ASSERT (`the dollars in` (`What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0)) TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the dollars in` (`What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the PV` 3 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0)
-- Bea (witness) and Carol (parent of a child victim) are both secondary victims: 22 491 in 2025-26, whatever the
-- number of offences.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the SV witness` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 22491 TRUE
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the SV parent` 2 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 22491 TRUE
-- Ed, father of an adult victim, a related victim: 11 245.50. The parent of a 17-year-old (a secondary victim) has
-- twice the related victim's maximum (NOTES.md finding 3).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the RV` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 11245.5 TRUE
#ASSERT `the dollars in` (`What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the SV parent` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0) EQUALS 2 TIMES `the dollars in` (`What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the RV` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0)
-- Gus paid for his brother's funeral; his sister has already been awarded $6 000 for the same funeral. The funeral
-- maximum is shared (s 6A(1B)): 11 245.50 - 6 000 = 5 245.50. Nothing is paid on top (s 6A(4) is only for future
-- services).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the FP` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 6000 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 5245.5 FALSE
-- If $12 000 has already been awarded for the funeral, nothing is left (never below 0).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the FP` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 12000 EQUALS `the most that may be awarded` 0 FALSE
-- Gus is also a related victim. The funeral maximum is outside s 6A(1) ("not including any amount that may be payable
-- under section 4(1A)"), so as both he may be awarded up to 11 245.50 + 11 245.50 = 22 491 (NOTES.md finding 4).
#ASSERT `the dollars in` (`What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the RV` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0) PLUS `the dollars in` (`What is the most I can be awarded for this application` `the FP` 1 `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2026` `the test CPI` 0) EQUALS 22491
